The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/types-physics/types-physics-05-incomplete-uom-typed-wrapper-coverage.md`. Here's a summary of the 6 findings:

| # | Severity | Summary |
|---|----------|---------|
| 1 | **High** | `uom` typed wrappers (`Temperature`, `Power`, `Energy`) are confined to `hares-physics`; all cross-crate interfaces (`PortContribution`, `PortSlots`, `ControlSignal`) use bare `f64` with name-suffix conventions |
| 2 | **Medium** | `PortContribution` mixes W (thermal/fuel) and kW (electrical) scales within a single enum, creating ~20+ manual `/1000` conversion points across equipment files |
| 3 | **Medium** | No custom `Add`/`Sub`/`Mul`/`Div` implementations with unit propagation — `Temperature × HeatCapacity` yields bare `f64`, not typed `Energy` |
| 4 | **Low** | `IDLE_KW_THRESHOLD` (named as kW constant) compared against watt-valued variables in `generator.rs:793,806` — semantically misleading, functionally harmless |
| 5 | **Low** | `SpecificHeatCapacity` and `MassDensity` `uom` types imported but not exposed as public aliases; `HeatCapacity` is exposed but `SpecificHeatCapacity` is not |
| 6 | **Low** | Typed boundary wrappers in `psychrometrics.rs`/`air_properties.rs` convert to/from `f64` at the crate boundary — no true type safety propagation downstream |
